  ('51', 51, false, 'Hub', '**accounts.md Owner/Recovery** — recorded 2026-09-26: Cloudflare, GitHub, Supabase under the secondary school Google account `falahacademykent@gmail.com`; EmailJS under the school Gmail. **Still needed:** recovery phone/email + 2-step method for BOTH school Google accounts; Brevo; GA4 (G-V6DNKDR9Z8 exists; which account owns it) + Search Console owner; Facebook page admins; WhatsApp admin; Bank of America online login; Red Comet / MESBA / iCode; OneDrive. **Then the first git commit of the hub** (on the President''s go) Priority lowered by the President 2026-09-26.', 'Muneeb (President) answers → Claude records', '2026-10-17', '2026-10-17', 'In progress', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('66', 66, false, 'Marketing', '**Entrance signage:** only an 11x17 banner marks the school at Al Huda. Get Al Huda''s OK, then order a portable A-frame or yard sign (about 24x36 in: logo, "Falah Academy", "Mon–Thu 9:00–2:00") for school days; check Kent''s portable-sign rules. While talking to Al Huda: ask them to correct the "Islamic School (Dugsi) Mon–Thu 9:00–1:00" line on alhudaislamiccenter.com/islamic-school (dugsi is weekends) and add a link to falahacademywa.org (was #25). Also photograph the entrance with the banner for the Google cover photo (#24)', 'Muneeb (President), Al Huda admin (Someone else)', 'next school visit', null, 'Parked', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('67', 67, false, 'Governance', '**File the 2027 WA SOS annual report** (CCFS, UBI 605 907 024; window opens 2026-12-02, expiration 2027-05-31; $20; Express filing works while status is Active). Save the report + receipt to `records/01_Corporate & Legal/03. Registrations & Certificates`', 'Muneeb (President)', '2027-04-30', '2027-04-30', 'Not started', null, '[{"name": "2026-09-25_WA-SOS_Annual-Report-2026_Filed_UBI-605907024.pdf", "path": "67/2026-09-25_WA-SOS_Annual-Report-2026_Filed_UBI-605907024.pdf", "size": 298079}, {"name": "2026-09-25_WA-SOS_Annual-Report-2026_Note.md", "path": "67/2026-09-25_WA-SOS_Annual-Report-2026_Note.md", "size": 1287}]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('69', 69, false, 'Website New Feature', '**Admissions: sibling fee plan + payment status — SHIPPED to prod 2026-09-28 (dev `5150fa3`).** Next to the "Sibling enrolled" badge the card shows a pill per sibling ("$300/mo · Sep paid ✓" / "Sep unpaid · 1 mo behind" / "starts …"); the dialog lists months paid of months owed this school year and the last payment date; the Monthly fee box defaults to **$200** with a "family rate" hint when a paying sibling is found (still editable). No SQL needed. Mark done once the President has seen it on a real applicant with an enrolled sibling.', 'Muneeb (Principal) verifies', '2026-11-30', '2026-11-30', 'Ready', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('77', 77, false, 'Portal', '**Tasks from the phone with photos — LIVE in prod (dev `3945f25`, prod `ca839b2`; phase 20 run in prod by the President 2026-09-30). Remaining: President adds a first task with a photo from the phone; Claude confirms it lands in TODO.md and `records/00_Inbox` on the next hourly pull.** Admin → Tasks "+ New task" (text, category, assignee, priority or date, notes, photos/PDFs) saves a P-coded row; the hourly Windows task "Falah Academy - task pull" (and `python scripts/todo-sync.py --pull prod --push all` by hand) copies it into TODO.md with a real number, moves files to `records/00_Inbox/` and removes the portal copies; done rows keep no files in the portal. **President:** run `dev/supabase/platform_schema_phase20.sql` in dev and add a task with a photo from the phone on the dev portal; then Claude mirrors to prod (the pull reads prod).', 'Claude → Muneeb (President) tests', '2026-10-10', '2026-10-10', 'In progress', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('79', 79, false, 'Bookkeeping', '**Record the September contractor pay in QBO:** five Zelle debits of 09-30 ($2,000 · $1,000 · $750 · $1,000 · $2,000 = $6,750) will appear in the …8048 bank feed within 1–2 business days → post each to Contract Labor - Teachers (1099), class Tuition Program, vendor = the person with "Track payments for 1099" on (create the four missing vendors; Qur''an teacher''s legal name still pending under #61); file the BofA alert emails in each `03. Payments` folder. **2026-09-30 (Claude, QBO in the pane):** bank feed refreshed — the five 09-30 debits have not arrived yet (feed still ends 09-28; 27 September items pending for #33). Vendors: the teachers already exist as payroll *employees*, so vendor names must differ → created **"<KG teacher> (Contractor)"** and **"<Pre-K teacher> (Contractor)"** with 1099 tracking on; the Grade 1 teacher''s vendor already existed (1099 tracking being switched on). All five vendors now ready (President confirmed 2026-09-30: the Pre-K teacher is a different person from the old "Shamsa Mugaza" vendor; the Qur''an teacher''s legal name = his portal name) — four "(Contractor)" vendors created with 1099 tracking, Grade 1 teacher''s pre-existing vendor already tracked; names listed in the pay-list note. **Open:** post the five debits when the feed shows them (bank still processing 09-30), then file the alert e-mails', 'Claude (Muneeb (accountant) signs in)', '2026-10-03', '2026-10-03', 'In progress', null, '[{"name": "2026-09-29_September_Contractor_Pay_List.md", "path": "79/2026-09-29_September_Contractor_Pay_List.md", "size": 6529}]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('84', 84, false, 'Academics', '**Red Comet weekly check-ins for all six Red Comet students (KG 3, Grade 1 2, Grade 3 1 — every KG+ student is with Red Comet; Pre-K is not).** Washington ALE rules from Red Comet''s orientation e-mails (two families forwarded theirs, 09-10 and 09-17, starred in the school Gmail under *Families & Admissions* + *Partners/Red Comet & MESBA*): a weekly attendance assignment in **every course**, a weekly login with visible progress, the Written Student Learning Plan completed first (it unlocks the course), Red Comet''s calendar not the school''s, withdrawal after 10 days counts as failed for grades 9–12. **Done so far:** the KG teacher received the three KG students'' Red Comet logins from the President on 10-01 (Gmail *Sent*, "Password and urls"). **Decide and do:** (1) the class teacher does the weekly check-in for her Red Comet students — confirm the Grade 1 / Grade 3 teacher also has her students'' logins; (2) where it is logged: portal Class Updates form or Red Comet''s own log, one place; (3) confirm all six have logged in and finished their Learning Plan, and that no weekly assignment is already overdue (school started 08-26, logins issued 09-10 onward); (4) reply to the two families who forwarded their e-mails and ask all six families to change the plain-text passwords once logged in. Feeds the teacher guide #87. (Closed by mistake 2026-10-04 and reopened the same evening.)', 'Muneeb (Principal)', '2026-10-15', '2026-10-15', 'In progress', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('87', 87, false, 'Academics', '**Write a one-page "Red Comet weekly check-in" guide for the KG and Grade 1 / Grade 3 teachers** (requested by the President 2026-10-04; pairs with #84 — six Red Comet students: KG 3, Grade 1 2, Grade 3 1): what a check-in is under Red Comet''s ALE rules, which students and which day each week, how to log in, where to see each student''s progress and overdue lessons, what to record (date, student, lessons done, concerns) and where (Class Updates form or a Red Comet log, per the #84 decision), when to escalate to the Principal, and who to contact at Red Comet. Source: the two Red Comet orientation e-mails of 09-10 and 09-17 (Gmail label *Partners/Red Comet & MESBA*, starred): weekly attendance assignment in **each course**, weekly login with visible progress, Written Student Learning Plan before anything else, Red Comet calendar rules, support alesupport@redcomet.com, FAQ redcomet.org/ale-faq, how-to video linked in the e-mail; plus the partner page. President reviews, then it goes to the teachers as PDF and into `records/15_Operations`', 'Claude drafts → Muneeb (Principal)', '2026-10-10', '2026-10-10', 'Not started', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('88', 88, false, 'Fundraising', '**Employer matching gifts — register the school so parents'' donations are doubled by their employers.** Microsoft, Boeing, T-Mobile, Costco, Starbucks, Expedia and others match employee gifts to 501(c)(3)s (Microsoft up to about $15,000 per employee a year, plus $25 per volunteer hour). Steps: (1) Claude prepares the pack: EIN 39-2254583, determination letter, mission text, W-9, bank details for ACH, logo; (2) President creates the school''s profile on **Benevity Causes** (causes.benevity.org) and **YourCause / Blackbaud** (solutions.yourcause.com/nonprofits) — account creation is the President''s step, Claude cannot do it; also claim the school on **Charity Navigator** and **GuideStar/Candid** so the portals verify faster; (3) once approved, Claude drafts the WhatsApp message and a Jumu''ah announcement for Al Huda: "ask HR whether your company matches gifts; donate through your company portal and the school receives double"; (4) record each matched gift in QBO as a donation (class Tuition Program or Scholarship). Needs #41 settled first', 'Claude prepares → Muneeb (President) registers', '2026-10-17', '2026-10-17', 'Not started', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('89', 89, false, 'Fundraising', '**Business sponsorship package for the fundraiser.** Claude drafts in `marketing/fundraiser-2026/sponsorship/`: (a) one-page tier sheet — Bronze $500, Silver $1,000, Gold $2,500, Platinum $5,000 — each giving name, logo, slogan and contact details on the flyer, event banner, website sponsors section and monthly newsletter (**acknowledgement only: no prices, no praise, no "call today"**, so every dollar stays a tax-free qualified sponsorship payment and the sponsor can deduct it); (b) a one-page sponsor letter signed by the President with the 501(c)(3) line and EIN; (c) a prospect list in `records/13_Marketing & Communication/` — Muslim-owned businesses in Kent, Renton, Tukwila, Seattle (restaurants, grocers, physicians, dentists, realtors, lawyers, car dealers) and the Islamic-finance / halal brands that sponsor Islamic schools: Saturna Capital / Amana Funds (Bellingham), Guidance Residential, UIF, Ijara CDC, Crescent Foods, Saffron Road, Zabihah; (d) a sponsors block for the website and the deck (#59). President reviews, then approaches the local businesses in person and the brands by e-mail. Every sponsorship over $250 gets a written acknowledgement letter for the sponsor''s taxes', 'Claude drafts → Muneeb (President) approaches', '2026-10-17', '2026-10-17', 'Not started', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('90', 90, false, 'Governance', '**Need-based scholarship policy + "Sponsor a student" ($300 a month or $3,000 a school year).** The website advertises need-based scholarships but no written policy or fund exists. Claude drafts a one-page policy (who qualifies, how a family applies, who decides — President + Treasurer, no board member''s own family, award = partial or full tuition for one school year, renewed yearly, confidential) and a sponsor-a-student one-pager for #89; the board adopts the policy by written consent together with #4; sponsor money is tracked in QBO under a *Scholarship Fund* class and awards are recorded in the portal as fee-plan adjustments. File in `records/10_Policies & Governance/`', 'Claude drafts → Muneeb (President) + board adopt', '2026-10-24', '2026-10-24', 'Not started', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('91', 91, false, 'Fundraising', '**Free in-kind programs now open with the 501(c)(3) letter:** Google for Nonprofits (Workspace, Ad Grants $10,000/month in search ads, YouTube) — apply through TechSoup validation (#34); Microsoft 365 nonprofit grant (free Business Basic seats) and Azure credits; **Fred Meyer Community Rewards** (families link their rewards card, the school gets a share of their grocery spend, nothing to the family); **Box Tops for Education** (enrol the school, families scan receipts in the app). Claude prepares each application and the two-line WhatsApp asks for families; President submits (accounts and consents are his step)', 'Claude prepares → Muneeb (President) submits', '2026-10-31', '2026-10-31', 'Not started', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('92', 92, false, 'Hiring', '**Volunteer program — set it up before the first volunteer walks in.** Six applicants were offered it on 2026-10-04 (#82, now D49) and five were asked for two references for the waiting list and the website mentions volunteering, but nothing exists on paper. Claude drafts: a one-page volunteer application (contact, availability, references, consent to a background check), the WA background check step (Washington State Patrol WATCH check, about $12 per person, plus the DCYF/national check if the volunteer is ever alone with children — ties to #42 Child Protection Policy), a one-page volunteer agreement (always under a teacher''s supervision, confidentiality of student information, photo rule, sign-in sheet), and a simple schedule template. Principal approves, then the two invited volunteers get the form with their visit date. File in `records/10_Policies & Governance/` and `records/16_Employees/00. Applicants & Waiting List/` **Drafts v1 ready 2026-10-05 (Claude):** four documents in `records/10_Policies & Governance/06. Volunteer Program/` as .docx + PDF — 01 Application Form, 02 Background Check Procedure (internal: references, WSP WATCH ≈ $12, nsopw.gov, fingerprint check only for unsupervised roles, decision rules, filing under `16_Employees/00. Volunteers/`), 03 Volunteer Agreement (never alone with a student, confidentiality, no photos, contact only via the school, reporting concerns), 04 Weekly Schedule + monthly Sign-in Sheet. Generator `scripts/make-volunteer-docs.py` (edit text there, re-run, Word makes the PDFs). **Principal:** review, decide 18+ only or 16–17 with parent signature, confirm the WATCH account is opened under the school Gmail, then send 01 + 03 to the invited volunteers with their visit date', 'Claude drafts → Muneeb (Principal) reviews', '2026-10-17', '2026-10-17', 'In progress', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('93', 93, false, 'Students', '**Special-needs student: written handling guidance for the teachers.** The student''s father will send the details (diagnosis, triggers, what helps, routines, emergency steps, who to call). When they arrive: Claude drafts a one-page classroom guidance sheet for the class teacher and the Pre-K assistant, the Principal reviews, the family confirms, and it goes into the student''s folder in `records/17_Students/` (not into the hub) and to the teachers only. Note in the portal student profile that guidance exists.', 'Muneeb (Principal); Claude drafts', 'when the father''s details arrive', null, 'Waiting', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('94', 94, false, 'Students', '**Create a WhatsApp group for the special-needs student: the student''s mother + class teacher + Pre-K assistant + Principal.** Purpose: daily notes both ways (how the morning went, anything the teachers should know), separate from the class group. Principal creates it, names it by the student''s first name only, and sets the ground rule (school-day messages, no photos of other children). Links with #93.', 'Muneeb (Principal)', '2026-10-10', '2026-10-10', 'Not started', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('95', 95, false, 'Website New Feature', '**Volunteer page + sign-up on the website.** New `volunteer.html` (why volunteer, what volunteers do — classroom support, reading groups, events, admin — requirements: 18+, background check, supervised at all times, a few hours a week) with a sign-up form in the same style as the admissions form: name, e-mail, phone, availability (days/times), skills or interests, how they heard of us, consent to a background check. The form e-mails the school Gmail via EmailJS **and** writes a row to a new portal table `volunteers` (Admin → Volunteers list, like applicants) so nothing is lost. Nav link in the footer and on the About page; links to the volunteer application and agreement from #92. Build in dev, mirror to prod per docs/dev-to-prod.md. **BUILT IN DEV 2026-10-05 (dev `fa8955a`, phase 22):** `volunteer.html` + `js/volunteer.js` (same form as the paper application: availability grid, interests, experience, two references, three disclosures, consent, under-18 parent block, honeypot) writes straight to `volunteer_applications`; nav dropdown + footer link on every page; sitemap. Admin → Volunteers: status flow New → Contacted → Screening → Approved → Active, dialog with all answers and the six dated screening checks, assigned class, notes; Dashboard tile. Every admin gets an in-app alert + immediate e-mail (needs the Brevo Vault key, else the daily dispatcher). No EmailJS copy — the portal alert replaces it. **President:** run `dev/supabase/platform_schema_phase22.sql` in the dev SQL editor, submit a test application on the dev site, check Admin → Volunteers; then Claude mirrors to prod.', 'Claude → Muneeb (President) tests', '2026-10-24', '2026-10-24', 'In progress', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('96', 96, false, 'Website New Feature', '**Admin alerts for class updates + Activity Calendar — BUILT IN DEV 2026-10-05 (dev `fa8955a`, phase 22).** (a) Every class update a teacher posts now creates an in-app notification for each admin ("Class update: Mathematics · KG — <teacher> posted…", link to Class Updates); the e-mail goes with the daily dispatcher so a busy day is one batch. (b) **Reworked 2026-10-05 on the President''s direction (dev `51a3462`): no separate page.** Admin → **Class Updates** now has a month calendar on top — every post is an event on its day ("KG: Mathematics", "G1: Science (child)", ★ = homework date), one color per grade (Pre-K rose, KG violet, Grade 1 blue, Grade 3 orange); clicking an event scrolls to the post below and highlights it; grade filter; ‹ › arrows through any past or future month. New Admin → **Attendance** page (under Students): month calendar of the whole school, one chip per grade per day with present+late / recorded and a red absence count; pick a student for their own green/amber/red days; click a day for the names. **President:** open both pages on the dev portal and say whether the colors and layout work; then Claude mirrors to prod.', 'Claude → Muneeb (President) tests', '2026-10-24', '2026-10-24', 'In progress', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('85', 85, false, 'Records', '**File three confirmations from the school Gmail into records:** FileLocal/Kent business-license application confirmation 9HXEXY4Q (09-24) → `01_Corporate & Legal/03. Registrations & Certificates` (also note the FileLocal "Originator ID" lines for accounts.md); L&I Q3 2026 report confirmation e-mail (09-30) → `04_…L&I/03. Quarterly Reports`; Intuit "E-pay and e-file are active" e-mail (10-01) → `05_Payroll`. Save each as PDF/markdown, then mark the thread *Filed*.', 'Claude', '2026-10-08', '2026-10-08', 'Not started', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('86', 86, false, 'Bookkeeping', '**QuickBooks subscription charge 10-01: $220.80** (QBO Plus at the new $140 price + Payroll Core + tax, per the Intuit receipt and the price-change notice in Gmail, label *QuickBooks & Payroll*). When the …8048 feed shows it, post as Software & Subscriptions, class Administration, and split the payroll portion if the receipt itemises it; check the amount matches what the President expected (QBO $140 + payroll tier). Folds into the October close.', 'Muneeb (accountant) + Claude', '2026-11-10', '2026-11-10', 'Not started', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('80', 80, false, 'W-2 payroll · B. Registrations', '**Payroll tax authorisations — update 2026-10-04 from the school Gmail: Intuit e-mail of 10-01 "E-pay and e-file are now active" → federal (941/EFTPS) authorisation approved and active; WA state agencies still to confirm.** Checked by Claude in QBO 2026-09-30: Payroll Overview shows all three setup items ticked (tax info, bank connected, "Authorize QuickBooks to handle your taxes"); the authorisation page reads "We''ve got your forms… you''ll hear from us once you''re all ready for online tax payments and filings. Until then you''re responsible for on-time payments and filings" → signed and received, **activation still pending with Intuit**; Payroll Tax Center shows nothing scheduled. Settings on file: Form 941 monthly depositor since 01/01/2026; WA UI 1.29% + EAF 0.02% (= the 1.31% notice), WA Cares 0.58%, PFML employee 71.43% / employer 0%; **WA L&I workers'' comp**: classes 6103-01 (0.4289 / 0.14455) and 6104-01 (1.0899 / 0.24235) effective 10/01/2026 but both marked *Inactive* and the L&I **Account ID field is empty** ("we need this account id to file your taxes") → add 511,674-00 there and activate the classes before the first payroll, or L&I stays manual (#28). **Still to do:** re-check the authorisation status in a few days (Intuit e-mails the school Gmail when active); President signs in to EAMS (SAW) so Claude can confirm the Q3 2026 no-payroll report (code G2E5C9B3FR7XJ0HM) shows accepted', 'Muneeb (accountant) + Claude', '2026-10-03', '2026-10-03', 'In progress', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('71', 71, false, 'Portal', '**Media-consent flags — LIVE in prod 2026-09-28** (dev `5150fa3`, prod `f025d4a`; phase 17 run in prod by the President; feature verified by Claude — student 10005''s signed form entered, badge reads "No public photos"). Student Profile shows a 📷 badge in the header ("Photos OK: public" · "Limited photo consent" · "No public photos" · "No photos at all" · "not on file") and an editable **Photo, Video & Media Consent** panel. **Remaining:** the other 14 students (10005, 10015 and 10003 entered from paper 2026-09-28; 10010 returned no consent form); until entered a student shows "not on file", which counts as no permission. Superseded in part by #73: families without an entered form are asked to fill it in the portal themselves.', 'Muneeb (Principal)', '2026-10-31', '2026-10-31', 'In progress', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('73', 73, false, 'Portal', '**Digital admission forms (Allergy · Medical · Photo/Media Consent) — LIVE in prod 2026-09-28** (dev `d206b45`, prod `280260e`; phase 18 run in prod by the President). Claude entered the two paper-form families'' Allergy + Medical forms through the admin dialog 2026-09-28 (all three forms show Completed for 10005 and 10015). **Open:** (a) President **re-runs the amended `platform_schema_phase18.sql` in prod** — office saves now count as reviewed, which clears the false "Updated by parent — review" flags on those six forms; (b) Vault secret `brevo_api_key` in prod (and dev) for the instant e-mail; (c) dev still needs phases 17 + 18 run. Original scope: Decisions 2026-09-28: portal forms replace paper for new families (not on the public website); families without an entered form see a reminder banner on the portal home (no pop-up) plus a Forms tab in Family Information; parents may update answers any time — every admin gets an in-app alert, and an **immediate e-mail** when an allergy, condition or medication is added or consent is withdrawn; Allergy and Medical are separate forms; immunizations stay a scanned certificate. Admin: Student Profile "Health & Consent Forms" card with status, summary, "Updated by parent — review" flag and Mark reviewed; a completed digital form ticks the Required Documents row. Phase 18 = medical_info form columns + per-form signature + review flag, parent write on media_consent, audit triggers, `notify_admins()` + `email_now()` (Brevo via pg_net, key from Vault). **President:** (1) run `dev/supabase/platform_schema_phase18.sql` in the dev SQL editor; (2) for the instant e-mail run once in the dev SQL editor `select vault.create_secret(''<BREVO_API_KEY value>'', ''brevo_api_key'');` (3) test as admin and as a parent on the dev portal; then Claude mirrors to prod. Follow-up: re-enter 10005 and 10015 through the new admin forms.', 'Claude → Muneeb (Principal) tests', '2026-10-10', '2026-10-10', 'In progress', null, '[]'::jsonb, now()),
  ('68', 68, false, 'Google / SEO', 'Ask 5–10 families for Google reviews — **parked by the President until after the second school year (summer 2027)**. WhatsApp draft ready: `marketing/whatsapp/2026-09_google-review-request.md`; link comes from the profile''s "Ask for reviews" button', 'Muneeb (President)', '2027-07-01', '2027-07-01', 'Parked', null, '[{"name": "2026-09_google-review-request.md", "path": "68/2026-09_google-review-request.md", "size": 1238}]'::jsonb, now()),
